d 'CORRHEAT': module to plot a correlation matrix as a heat map with r and p labels and a color bar
d
d  corrheat creates correlational matrix heat plots (lower-triangle
d portion only) in a single command. It runs pwcorr on the
d specified variables, labels each cell with its correlation
d coefficient and p-value, and draws a gradient color bar using the
d same colors and cut points as the cells. All cell labels follow
d APA style by default (no leading zeros, p < .001), and the label
d text switches to white on dark cells for legibility (white text
d cutoffs are adjustable). Options control the color palette, the
d bin cut points (so several figures can share one scale), label
d sizes, bar position and ticks, and pairwise or listwise deletion.
d Any other twoway options are passed through to the graph, and the
d user's data are left unchanged. 
d
d KW: correlation
d KW: correlation matrix
d KW: heat map
d KW: heatplot
d KW: graphics
d
d Requires: Stata version 16 and heatplot, palettes, colrspace from SSC (q.v.)
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261125
d
d Author: Shane Littrell ,  Cornell University
d Support: email shane.littrell27@@gmail.com
d
f corrheat.ado
f corrheat.sthlp
f corrheat.pdf
